                                "sense_id": "9a0838f0-b139-3e22-880a-7e654b152562",
                                "text": "Featy adj. 2. This word expressed a particular kind of injury to which wool or woollen cloth is liable if left long in the damp - it seems to be rotten as to strength, while in appearance there is little change."
